// EXPECT: E0268 — an imported `$N` specialization still needs cross-file comptime evaluation (ADR-0230)
//
// ADR-0230 lifts ADR-0104's blanket refusal for imported pure `$T` procedures. A `$N` template is a different
// operation: its argument must first be evaluated as a compile-time value, and that cross-file const-eval
// dependency is deliberately outside this wave.
//
// `Generic.identity($T)` remains in the fixture as the historical pure-type case, and
// `imports/valid/022-cross-file-generic-procedure.jr` now exercises that capability through the bundled
// `Generic_Types` module. This file keeps exactly one refusal and pins the narrower remaining boundary.
#import "Generic";

main :: () {
  // `scaled` is a `$N` template in another module. Imported compile-time values remain E0268.
  n := scaled(5, 6);
}
